.TH HD-LOGO 6 "November 2026" "hd-screensavers" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-logo \- the bouncing logo screensaver of HyprDebian
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-logo
.RB [ \-\-framerate
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-window ]
.br
.B hd-logo \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-logo
is the moving logo of the old DVD players, a screensaver of the package
.BR hd-screensavers :
the Debian swirl with \(lqHyprDebian\(rq over it, bouncing on black and
changing colour at each bounce.
It is light on the GPU and the battery.
.PP
Every monitor has a logo of its own.
The logo moves at exactly 45\(de, one step on both axes per tick, at
.B \-\-framerate
ticks a second, and lands on the edges exactly.
Its height is near 20% of the height of the monitor, and the step near 10
heights of the monitor per minute, among the sizes and steps where the step
divides the distances the logo can travel; so the speed on the screen is the
same at any frame rate.
It starts at a random place, in a random direction, on a path that passes a
corner, sooner or later.
At an edge it bounces and takes the next colour; a corner, where it reaches
two edges on the same tick, is a bounce too.
.PP
The colours are
.BR normal ,
.B highlight
and
.B light
of the theme, in that order, from the key
.B hd-theme
of the configuration: that of the user first, then that of the system.
A colour that is missing has its value of the theme
.BR default .
They are read at the start.
.PP
It puts a surface on the overlay layer of every monitor, of
wlr-layer-shell, with the keyboard to itself, and follows the monitors that
come and go while it runs.
It ends on a key press, a move of the mouse, a click, a scroll or a touch,
and on SIGTERM or SIGINT.
The pointer that is on a monitor when it starts does not end it; the
cursor is hidden.
.PP
It draws with Vulkan, one textured quad per monitor without multisampling,
on the GPU that drives the compositor, the main device of its dmabuf
feedback.
When the compositor names none, or that GPU will not do, it is the first
discrete GPU that can show on the compositor, else an integrated one, else
a virtual one, else lavapipe of mesa-vulkan-drivers, which renders on the
CPU.
It needs Vulkan 1.3, or Vulkan 1.2 with VK_KHR_dynamic_rendering and
VK_KHR_synchronization2.
.PP
.B hd-launch-screensaver
of
.B hd-desktop
starts it, without arguments, when the key
.B hd-screensaver
of the configuration names it, see
.BR hd-screensaver (7):
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo hd-config-update hd-screensaver '"hd-logo"'
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-framerate " N"
The ticks per second on each monitor, 1 to 1000, or 0 for a tick at every
refresh of each monitor, from its current mode.
A frame is drawn at each tick.
It sets the step too, so the speed on the screen stays the same; fewer
ticks take less of the GPU and move the logo in bigger steps.
Default: 30.
.TP
.B \-\-window
One ordinary window instead of every monitor, with the app id
.BR hd-logo ,
which input does not end; Escape or closing the window ends it.
The logo starts again when the window is resized.
It is not read from the configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the options with their ranges and defaults, and exit.
.PP
Each option is
.BI \-\- name " value"
or
.BI \-\- name = value\fR.
When an option is given more than once, the last wins.
The size, the speed and the colours are not options.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The key
.B hd-logo
of the configuration sets the frame rate too:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{"hd-logo": {"framerate": 60}}
.fi
.RE
.PP
It is read in the configuration of the system,
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
and then in that of the user,
.IR ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json ;
the one of the user wins.
Run as root, it only reads the configuration of the system.
The command line wins over both.
See
.BR hd-config (7).
.PP
A value out of its range or of the wrong type, a member that is not an
option, a key that is not an object and a file that is not valid JSON are
reported on stderr and skipped, so the value below stays.
On the command line a wrong value is an error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
It ended, on input, on SIGTERM or SIGINT, or after
.BR \-\-help .
.TP
.B 1
It cannot start: no Vulkan device, no wlr-layer-shell, no monitors; or it
lost the compositor.
The reason is on stderr.
.TP
.B 2
A wrong argument.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json
The configuration of the user, with the keys
.B hd-logo
and
.BR hd-theme .
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The configuration of the system, with the keys
.BR hd-logo ,
.B hd-theme
and
.BR hd-screensaver .
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/hd-screensavers/copyright
The notice of the Debian Open Use Logo, which the swirl is.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-pipes (6),
.BR hd-screensaver (7),
.BR hd-config (7),
.BR hypridle (1)
